<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">455 CE</h1><p class="ref-lede">455 CE in world history: 5 events and 1 death. 162 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/435">435 CE</a><a href="/years/439">439 CE</a><a href="/years/451">451 CE</a><a href="/years/454">454 CE</a><a href="/years/455" aria-current="page">455 CE</a><a href="/years/474">474 CE</a><a href="/years/475">475 CE</a><a href="/years/476">476 CE</a><a href="/years/484">484 CE</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/valentinian-iii" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/valentinian-iii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-17">17 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Petronius Maximus takes the throne of the Western Roman Empire</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">With the support of the Senate, Maximus secured the throne after the murder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valentinian-iii">Valentinian III</a> by paying palace officials, and married the reluctant widow Licinia Eudoxia. He reigned only 75 days before a mob killed him as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vandals">Vandals</a> neared <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valentinian-iii">Valentinian III</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-31">31 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Petronius Maximus is killed by a mob while fleeing Rome</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">As a Vandal fleet under Geiseric sailed for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, the Western Roman emperor Petronius Maximus rode out of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> alone and was stoned to death by an angry mob after 75 days on the throne. Three days later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vandals">Vandals</a> took Rome and sacked it.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/vandals" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vandals.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-2">2 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Vandals begin a two-week sack of Rome</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">King Gaiseric's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vandals">Vandals</a> entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and plundered it for fourteen days, carrying off treasure and captives to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>. The episode later gave the word 'vandalism' to European languages.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vandals">Vandals</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/visigoths.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-9">9 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Avitus is acclaimed Western Roman Emperor near Arles</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Backed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> and the Gallo-Roman nobility, the senator <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avitus">Avitus</a> was acclaimed emperor near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arles">Arles</a>. His reign lasted barely a year, a sign of how weak the Western Empire had become.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a></div></div></li></ol></section>
